A||||11||artherd||13" Held Motorsports brakes||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||06-29-2001||07:32 AM||||Just wondering if anyone on the fourm has the new 13" setup from Ryane/Held.<P>I've driven a car with their 12" setup, and uh, wow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>What do the 13s with their one-piece rotors add to unsprung weight?<P>I'm trying to decide between the two.<P>Thanks!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-29-2001||02:31 PM||||I would imagine it depends how you use the car. <P>If you race it at high speeds (1/4mi, road race) I would think the 13's might be agood investment, if you autocross, I'd think the 12"s would be more than enough. <P>Also, what are you running for HP? If it's under 225hp, I'd simply upgrade the stock equip (add lines, pads, better fluid), anything over that, I'd go at least the 12"s. <P>OH, you WILL need bigger wheels, too. Now, there are 11" 4-piston kits out there...they will fit inside most 15" wheels, and still rule!<BR>Email if you need more info on those...<P>Good luck! <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">  <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||06-29-2001||03:11 PM||||There is not much need to upgrade brakes on the '88s unless you have a serious upgrade in engine performance. I have run several track days in the last month with the stock brakes and, street performance pads and Ford spec brake fluid. They have peformed fade free with minimal wear during more than an hour of  track time. You will find that just upgrading to some serious performance pads will substantialy improve braking performance. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||06-29-2001||03:17 PM||||Well if you have the money to afford the 12 inch upgrade, then just go for the 13's, it's only like 250 bucks more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Plus they look better!   <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||06-29-2001||05:11 PM||||Won’t the 13 inch brakes have a tendency to just lock up. IT would be overkill without ABS or huge tires wouldn’t it? <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||06-29-2001||10:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Won’t the 13 inch brakes have a tendency to just lock up...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Not necessarilly...they would provide greater fade-resistance. Sure, you'd have more stopping power, that's what pedal-feedback and experience are for, the real benefit would be in continued braking ability after repeated long, high speed braking sessions, like a road course. Also, with a V8 swap, or other weight increase, you might just need the added braking capability, even short-term. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||sjp777||06-29-2001||11:29 PM||||You need 17" rims to go with the 13" brakes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||06-30-2001||04:52 AM||||A quick update, I do have 17" (or rather will very shortly, thanks Trav! :) wheels/tyres, and by the time this all happens (read: by the time I have the $ :) the car will have Held coilovers and a 300bhp Northstar V8.<P>The reasons for upgrading are twofold:<BR>I'd be a fool IMHO to more than double the horsepower in a car and not touch the brakes.<P>The 88 brakes are always sticking and binding in my expierence, and I'm sick of replacing them :) (not a big fan of single piston calipers)<P>Anyway, anyone with either the 12" or 13" Held/Ryane system?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||JayUSA77||07-01-2001||01:07 AM||||Hey guys where can i get these brakes?????<BR>-J<BR>86 Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||sjp777||07-01-2001||01:20 AM||||Right here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com/brake13.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com/brake13.htm</A> <P>Hope your checking account is brimming with money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||07-01-2001||01:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JayUSA77:<BR><B>Hey guys where can i get these brakes?????<BR>-J<BR>86 Fiero GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com</A> <P>I used to own a heavily modified '85 GT with Ryane's (now Held) slalom one coilover kit, '88 rear cradle & the 12" brakes.   All I can say is WOW!  Those brakes are awesome and well worth the $$ if you plan on adding a lot more horsepower. I can only imagine that the 13" ones are just as good (they at least look better). <P>BTW.....I had thse 12" brakes under stock '86-'87 GT 15" wheels!  Believe it or not.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
